# Brain Arcade — Supabase project credentials.
#
# Copy this file to client/.env.local and fill in your project's actual
# values (Supabase dashboard → Connect, or Project Settings → API Keys).
# Never commit the real file — .env.local is already gitignored via the
# root *.local rule.
#
# Note: Supabase renamed these — what used to be called the "anon" key is
# now the "publishable" key (same kind of value: safe to expose in client
# code, not a secret).
#
# IMPORTANT: the Supabase dashboard's "Connect" snippet defaults to Next.js
# naming — NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL / NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY.
# This app is Vite, not Next. Copy the VALUES, but the VARIABLE NAMES must
# be exactly VITE_SUPABASE_URL / VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY below — Vite
# only exposes vars prefixed VITE_ to the app at all. Get this wrong and
# there's no error: Brain Arcade just silently stays unconfigured.
#
# Until these are set, Brain Arcade's Supabase calls no-op gracefully
# (see client/src/arcade/supabase.ts) — the rest of the app works fine.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-key
